2:T15a9,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Where can I buy a genuine EcoFlow power station in Kenya?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You can buy genuine EcoFlow power stations in Kenya from Batteriq (batteriq.com), the authorised EcoFlow dealer based in Nairobi. Batteriq delivers to all 47 counties and accepts M-Pesa and Visa/Mastercard. Every unit is genuine stock with the full manufacturer warranty, supported locally in Kenya. Every order comes with an official eTIMS (KRA) invoice, which businesses can use for tax records."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where can I buy BLUETTI power stations in Kenya?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Batteriq sells BLUETTI power stations in Kenya online at batteriq.com/bluetti, with M-Pesa payment and delivery from Nairobi to all 47 counties."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does an EcoFlow power station cost in Kenya?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"EcoFlow power stations in Kenya range from compact RIVER models for phones, laptops and Wi-Fi up to DELTA Pro whole-home systems. Current Kenya shilling prices for every model are listed live on batteriq.com. Smaller RIVER units suit lights, phones, laptops and routers. DELTA models run fridges, TVs and power tools. DELTA Pro and home systems back up most of a house."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I pay for a power station with M-Pesa in Kenya?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Batteriq accepts M-Pesa through an STK Push prompt at checkout: you enter your phone number, confirm the prompt on your phone with your M-Pesa PIN, and the order is paid instantly. Visa and Mastercard are also accepted through Paystack (a 2% card processing fee applies to card payments only). Cash on Delivery and M-Pesa on Delivery are available on eligible orders."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the best backup power for KPLC blackouts in Kenya?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For most Kenyan homes, a portable power station with an LFP battery (such as EcoFlow DELTA or BLUETTI) is the best blackout backup: it switches on silently, needs no fuel, runs indoors, and can be recharged from KPLC power or solar panels. Unlike a petrol generator there are no fumes, no noise and no fuel runs. Unlike a traditional inverter with lead-acid batteries, LFP power stations last thousands of cycles and need no maintenance."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What size power station do I need for my home in Kenya?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Add up the watts of everything you want to run, multiply by the hours you need them, and choose a power station whose capacity (Wh) is about 20% above that total and whose output (W) is above the combined load. Example: a fridge (~150 W) + TV (~100 W) + lights (~50 W) + Wi-Fi (~15 W) is about 315 W. For 6 hours that is roughly 1,900 Wh, so a 2,000–2,500 Wh unit is a good fit. Batteriq will size a system for free — send your appliance list on WhatsApp (+254 716 822 014)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a power station run a fridge in Kenya?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Mid-size and larger EcoFlow DELTA and BLUETTI power stations run a household fridge for many hours, because a typical fridge only draws around 100–200 W once it is running. Choose a unit whose output is well above the fridge’s start-up surge; DELTA-class models handle this comfortably."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can an EcoFlow power station work as a UPS during power cuts?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. EcoFlow power stations support pass-through charging and switch over automatically when KPLC power drops, so Wi-Fi routers, desktops and CCTV keep running through a blackout."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is a power station better than a petrol generator in Kenya?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For home and office backup, yes: a power station is silent, fume-free, safe indoors and has no fuel costs. A petrol generator is only better for very long outages with very heavy loads where solar recharging is not possible."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I charge a power station with solar panels in Kenya?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Kenya gets roughly 5–6 peak sun hours a day in most regions, so EcoFlow and BLUETTI power stations can be fully recharged by compatible solar panels in a single sunny day."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does an EcoFlow battery last?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Current EcoFlow power stations use LFP (lithium iron phosphate) batteries rated for 3,000+ charge cycles to 80% capacity — roughly 10 years of daily use."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Batteriq deliver outside Nairobi?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Batteriq delivers across Nairobi and ships nationwide by courier to all 47 counties in Kenya."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What warranty do EcoFlow products have in Kenya?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"EcoFlow power stations bought from Batteriq carry a 24-month warranty, handled locally in Kenya by Batteriq as the authorised dealer. Register your product online so a future warranty claim is fast."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I contact Batteriq?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Call or WhatsApp Batteriq on +254 716 822 014, or email info@batteriq.com. The team is available Monday to Saturday, 8am–6pm Nairobi time, and you can place an order online at any time."}}]}11:{"size":20}
